* Stub vdW parameters for protein/lipid atom types referenced in NBFIX
* entries of toppar_water_ions_cufix.str.
*
* These residue types are NEVER present in a DNA+water+Mg2+ simulation.
* NAMD3 validates ALL NBFIX pairs whose first atom type (OTMG, OTCA, SOD,
* POT, NH3, …) is present in the PSF — which requires BOTH members to have
* defined vdW parameters.  Without these stubs, NAMD exits with "DIDN'T FIND
* vdW PARAMETER FOR ATOM TYPE OC/OG2P1/NH3/…" whenever MGH is present.
*
* Missing types: OC OCL OC2D2 OC2DP OG2D2 OG2P1 O2L NH3 NH3L NC2 NG3P3 NP NR3
* Values approximate CHARMM36 protein/lipid parameters.  Exact values do not
* affect DNA+water+Mg physics because these atoms are absent from the PSF.
*

NONBONDED  NBXMOD 5  ATOM CDIEL FSHIFT VATOM VDISTANCE VFSWITCH -
cutnb 14.0 ctofnb 12.0 ctonnb 10.0 eps 1.0 e14fac 1.0 wmin 1.5

! Oxygen types (protein carboxylate, lipid carbonyl/ester/phosphate)
OC       0.000000  -0.120000     1.700200  ! carboxylate O (par_all36_prot.prm)
OCL      0.000000  -0.120000     1.700200  ! lipid carbonyl O
OC2D2    0.000000  -0.120000     1.700200  ! ester carbonyl O
OG2D2    0.000000  -0.120000     1.700200  ! aldehdye/ketone O (CHARMM36c)
O2L      0.000000  -0.121000     1.768200  ! lipid phosphate O
OG2P1    0.000000  -0.120000     1.700000  ! phosphate O (CHARMM36c/m)
OC2DP    0.000000  -0.120000     1.700000  ! phosphate O (CHARMM36c)

! Nitrogen types (protein/lipid amine, guanidinium, ring N)
NH3      0.000000  -0.200000     1.850000  ! protonated amine (Lys NH3+)
NH3L     0.000000  -0.200000     1.850000  ! lipid amine (CHARMM36 lipid)
NC2      0.000000  -0.200000     1.850000  ! guanidinium N (Arg)
NG3P3    0.000000  -0.200000     1.850000  ! amine N (CHARMM36c)
NP       0.000000  -0.200000     1.850000  ! protonated amine N
NR3      0.000000  -0.200000     1.850000  ! aromatic/imidazole N

END
